  "version": "0.32.2",
  "notes": "### Fixed\n\n- **A stopped phone run keeps its worker until it has really ended.** Ten seconds after Stop, the link used to give the run's worker to the next job even when the agent was still running, so new work could start beside it. It now waits for the run to end, and Activity says \"Stop requested · waiting for the agent to finish ending\" meanwhile; restarting Mimir still ends it as Interrupted.\n- **Stopped means the same however the agent ends.** A run that ended quietly after Stop now carries the same \"check any partial changes\" note as one that ended with an error, and its old step line is cleared.\n- **Real progress is told apart from signs of life.** Each phone run now reports when it last made progress (words or a step), apart from the lane's own routing lines, and the snapshot gives exact counts of waiting and stopping runs, so the phone never counts from the newest 150 alone.",
